                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 15 at 10:28PM CDT until September 16 at 4:30AM CDT by NWS Quad Cities IA IL",
                "description": "FFWDVN\n\nThe National Weather Service in Quad Cities has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nWest Central Lee County in southeastern Iowa...\nNorthwestern Clark County in northeastern Missouri...\nCentral Scotland County in northeastern Missouri...\n\n* Until 430 AM CDT Wednesday.\n\n* At 1028 PM CDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1.5 inches are\npossible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nFort Madison, Memphis, Donnellson, Montrose, Luray, Granger,\nCroton, New Boston, Crawford, Revere, Arbela, Chambersburg, Ashton,\nHeath Memorial Conservation Area, Anson, Prospect Grove, Etna,\nPeaksville and Battle of Athens Campground.",
